<title>USA: Twin City Bancorp sets 3-for-2 stock split.</title>
<headline>Twin City Bancorp sets 3-for-2 stock split.</headline>
<dateline>BRISTOL, Tenn. 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Twin City Bancorp Inc said Monday it has set a three-for-two stock split.</p>
<p>The split will be payable in the form of a 50 percent stock dividend. The new shares are to be payable on September 8 to stockholders of record as of August 25.</p>
<p>President Thad Bowers said in a statement that the stock dividend was set to increase the trading activity and liquidity of the company's stock.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
</text>
